# The theme is not set here: it depends on the terminal's background, which only
# bin/theme knows. bin/_bat exports BAT_THEME per call and every script in bin/
# goes through it. bat's own auto:system read the macOS setting rather than the
# terminal, and warned loudly off the Mac — straight into the fzf preview pane.

# Expand tabs to two columns. bat does this itself only on a terminal; piped into
# a pager (_bat-at, the fzf previews) the raw tabs reach less, which stops every
# eight columns off the line-number gutter — nesting balloons.
--tabs=2
